# Citation metadata in Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# Everything below is taken from the repository itself: the authorship recorded in
# `git log`, the attribution line in README.md, and the remote configured for `origin`.
# No DOI, ORCID or additional author is claimed, because the repository substantiates none.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "biodao.blockchain"
abstract: >-
  A local molecular workspace for drug discovery that runs in a WebXR headset or an
  ordinary browser. It loads experimental structures from the RCSB PDB and predicted
  structures from the AlphaFold database, detects and ranks binding pockets, performs
  flexible Monte Carlo docking scored by a Vina-style empirical function, runs
  interactive coarse-grained dynamics in the browser and all-atom implicit-solvent
  dynamics with OpenMM on the local machine, and gathers target evidence from public
  biomedical databases. It curates sixty targets across amyotrophic lateral sclerosis,
  Parkinson's disease, other neurogenetic disorders, conditions treated by Shriners
  Children's, and apoptosis. Docking scores are intended for triage and ranking, not as
  predicted binding affinities; placeholder values that no engine computed are marked
  as synthetic in both their textual form and their provenance field.
